WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.868
-The New York attorney
general announced today

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.601
that her office is suing
Donald Trump

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.234
to bar him from doing business
in the state over allegations

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.534
what she called
staggering fraud.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.534
The announcement comes a day
after a special master

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.067
chastised Trump's legal team
during a hearing

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.868
on the classified documents he
allegedly stashed at Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.467
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:24.467
♪♪

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.000
Right now, we're
in a pretty stunning situation

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.100
where the two leading contenders
for the 2024 GOP nomination

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.801
have both sparked lawsuits
and criminal investigations.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.567
Authorities in Texas announced
they're opening a probe

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.267
into Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis'

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.767
repulsive scheme to lure
migrants onto a plane from Texas

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.701
under false pretenses and strand
them on Martha's Vineyard.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:47.300
And now the migrants have also
filed a class action lawsuit

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.267
against DeSantis alleging fraud.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.968
It's almost as
if they're competing to see

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.234
who could be more corrupt.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.467
As "Rolling Stone"
reported recently...

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:09.634
I can't even begin to imagine
what that would look like.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.868
Walls on both borders?

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.300
Hats that say "Make America
even more greater again

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.234
times infinity"?

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.667
Remember when Trump
used to hug the flag

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:23.534
at his speeches like a tourist
riding the New York City subway

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:24.934
for the first time?

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.834
If Ron DeSantis
tries to top that,

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.934
he's likely end up
doing something so obscene

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.801
we'd have to blur it.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.534
Now, these guys clearly already
have a lot in common.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.067
The shameless lying,
bullying, open bigotry,

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.901
performative spectacles
of cruelty,

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:43.300
obsessive focus on bull[Bleep]
culture war nonsense,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.868
even the way they stand
is incredibly weird.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:50.467
What is going on here?

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.834
That's the way
a stoned teenager stands

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.834
when his mom
comes home unexpectedly.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.367
Mother, uh, you're home.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.801
What happened at book club?

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.901
Mrs. Daldry has a cold?
For shame.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.501
Well...

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:15.567
...I'm off to bed.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.701
Is it only 6:30?

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:17.734
Well...

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.901
...the early bird catches
the proverbial worm

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:26.567
or so they say
in the proverb.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.701
At least with Trump, you can
kind of tell what's going on --

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.200
puffing his chest out
to seem manly,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.801
but ends up looking like
he's trying to record

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:34.067
all his conversations
with a secret microphone

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.234
strapped to his chest.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.300
[ Imitating Trump ]
And just what was that

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.801
you said about election fraud?

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.467
Can you say it louder
and closer to my nipples?

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:44.868
[ Normal voice ]
But for the life of me,

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.834
I just cannot figure out

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.067
what is going on
in this picture with DeSantis.

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:52.601
He looks like an off-brand
G.I. Joe action figure

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:55.701
you'd get for Christmas
from your grandma

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.100
in a box labeled,
I don't know, "Swamp Man".

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:01.133
He looks like a character

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:04.567
who gives you your mission
in "Grand Theft Auto".

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:07.734
[ Deep voice ] Hey. Hey, Tony.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:11.167
I need you to go down
to the docks

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:14.767
and trick some migrants into
flying to Martha's Vineyard.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Normal voice ] Why does he
look so nervous all the time?

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:22.834
He reminds me of Ralph Kramden
on "The $99,000 Answer".

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:23.934
I'm really sorry, you guys.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:26.667
NBC is pushing us
to appeal to Gen Z,

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.200
and audience research tells us

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.901
that the things 20 year olds
love the most are "Fortnite",

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.434
TikTok, and episodes
of "The Honeymooners".

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.934
I don't know.

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:39.400
I guess it was like
the 1950s "Euphoria".

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.534
I've been told -- I don't --
They just hand us research.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:47.000
So these two undercover
Men's Warehouse mannequins

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.033
now have another thing
in common.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.300
They both sparked lawsuits
and criminal investigations.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.467
But if DeSantis thought
he could catch up to Trump

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.133
in the crime department, he's
still got a long way to go,

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:59.167
because today Trump got hit with
yet another legal bombshell.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.667
New York Attorney General
Letitia James announced

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.467
that her office is suing Trump
and his family over allegations

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.567
of long-running
and staggering fraud.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:08.934
-New York state attorney general
announcing moments ago

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.601
her office is suing
the former president,

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:14.567
his adult children,
and the Trump Organization

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.033
for what her office describes
as bank, tax,

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.767
and insurance fraud.

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:23.734
-We show that they violated
several state criminal laws,

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:28.100
including falsifying
business records,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.567
issuing false
financial statements,

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:32.934
insurance fraud.

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:35.300
We believe the conduct
alleged in this section

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.200
also violates
federal criminal law,

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.901
including issuing
false statements

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:44.934
to financial institutions
and bank fraud.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:48.000
We are requiring Mr. Trump
and the Trump Organization

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.934
to disgorge the financial
benefits obtained through

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:54.267
the persistent fraudulent
practices an estimated,

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:58.901
a baseline at the minimum
of $250 million.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:01.133
-Whoa, $250 million.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.100
To pay that, he'd probably
have to sell Mar-a-Lago

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.234
and move in with Rudy.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.300
[ Imitating Trump ]
I got top bunk.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.634
Rudy, you got bottom.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.000
[ Imitating Giuliani ]
But there's only the one bed.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.501
[ Imitating Trump ] That's
right, you sleep on the floor

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.834
under the mattress
and keep an eye --

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:18.434
you keep an eye out for bedbugs,
Rudy, I'm counting on you.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:20.100
[ Normal voice ] I doubt Trump
can afford to just fork

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.634
over $250 million.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.133
Something tells me
his supporters are about

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.934
to get a bunch of frantic
e-mails that say...

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.334
The lawsuit also named Trump's
three oldest children,

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.367
and you know what that means?

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:37.701
Today is a good time
to meet Tiffany.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:41.000
I -- I'm sure there were times

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.033
you were upset not to be
in the inner circle, girl,

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.767
but when the attorney general
doesn't say your name,

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.934
it's a good day.
Live your life.

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:49.234
Of course, even before
this bombshell announcement,

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:51.834
Trump was also facing multiple
criminal investigations

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:53.601
for the attempted coup
on January 6th,

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.767
and perhaps more prominently,
the classified documents

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.267
he apparently stole
from the White House

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:00.734
and stashed away
at his private beach club.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:03.934
Now, there's no way of knowing
if Trump broke the law,

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.434
except he definitely did,
and it's [Bleep] crazy

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:08.501
we have to entertain
the idea he didn't.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.534
No one loses a job
and gets to take

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.300
whatever they want
on the way out the door,

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.934
especially if you work
for the government.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.868
It's pack up your things,
not, "You're fired.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:18.868
Take whatever mementos
you'd like as a token

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:21.100
of our appreciation for
the [Bleep] job you did."

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.200
Also, no one's buying
your excuse

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.868
that you had to pack
at the last minute.

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:26.968
There's a reason we elect
a new president in November

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.033
and give the old one
until January to move out.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:30.767
Of course, Trump spent
those two months

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.400
convinced the election
was gonna get overturned.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.901
He probably stood over Melania

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.734
while she was putting clothes
in a suitcase, saying

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:37.100
[ Imitating Trump ] "I don't
know why you're doing that.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.534
You're just gonna have to put
them back in the drawer

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:41.634
when Mike Pence refuses
to certify the election."

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:42.701
[ Normal voice ] She's like
[ Imitating Melania ]

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:43.701
Donald, please,
I want to get this done.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:45.000
Don't wait
till the last minute."

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.968
[ Normal voice ] And then
the morning of the inauguration,

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:48.300
Melania was yelling
into the Oval Office,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.801
"The helicopter is here,"
and he was just running around

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.300
throwing documents
into a duffel bag, yelling,

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.400
[ Imitating Trump ]
"On my way, Mel, on my way.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.634
I'm just -- Oh, I'm writing
a note to Joe Biden

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:59.834
wishing him luck -- Oh [Bleep]

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.434
[Bleep] I don't know
what I'm allowed to --

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.767
I'll take everything,
I'll take everything."

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:05.934
[ Normal voice ] Now,
one of the keys to proving

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:07.234
to the court
that Trump broke the law --

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:09.133
in particular
that he obstructed justice

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:10.767
or violated the Espionage Act,

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:13.067
which was cited by the DOJ
in its warrant

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:15.200
to search Mar-a-Lago --
is demonstrating

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.434
that Trump willfully retained
national defense information

00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:19.667
he knew he shouldn't have.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.167
And this week,
we got some bombshell reporting

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:22.534
from "The New York Times"
revealing

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:25.501
that Trump was told
he was in legal jeopardy

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:28.200
if he kept the documents,
and he kept them anyway.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.067
-"The New York Times"
is reporting tonight

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:33.033
that a former
White House counsel warned

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:37.567
Donald Trump last year when he
was no longer president that...

00:08:02.901 --> 00:08:04.701
-Of course Trump knew
he was committing a crime.

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.467
He didn't take the documents
by accident.

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:07.834
He's not Cap'n Crunch.

00:08:07.834 --> 00:08:09.634
The box he took from
the White House didn't say

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:12.601
"Oops! All classified".

00:08:12.601 --> 00:08:15.267
They were clearly marked
"all classified",

00:08:15.267 --> 00:08:17.067
some of them were part
of the nuclear documents.

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:18.367
You don't take those
by accident,

00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:20.234
and if you do,
you return them ASAP.

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:22.534
It's not like when
you're hastily moving out

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:24.167
of an apartment
you shared with an ex

00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:26.300
and you realize
after you move out

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.934
that you accidentally
took her old college sweater,

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:32.267
and it makes you
sort of wistful,

00:08:32.267 --> 00:08:35.434
and you can't help but
reminisce, you know,

00:08:35.434 --> 00:08:37.133
about all the good times
you had together --

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:40.033
that first time you held hands
in a movie theater,

00:08:40.033 --> 00:08:43.067
when you drove her home
from a friend's party

00:08:43.067 --> 00:08:46.501
and just sat in the driveway,

00:08:46.501 --> 00:08:48.200
or that time
you got a little too tipsy

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.334
in a Lower East Side dive bar

00:08:50.334 --> 00:08:52.901
and walked around the city until
the early hours of the morning,

00:08:52.901 --> 00:08:55.567
the sun peeking out
over the Brooklyn Bridge

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:58.234
and the Hudson,

00:08:58.234 --> 00:09:01.734
simmering with the new light
of a hopeful morning.

00:09:01.734 --> 00:09:03.501
So you decided to text her
one last time

00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:08.501
just to -- just to say hi,
just to say you miss her,

00:09:08.501 --> 00:09:12.801
that this might be a mistake,
that you're not --

00:09:12.801 --> 00:09:15.167
you're not ready to move on.

00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:16.367
And then she responds...

00:09:18.734 --> 00:09:20.133
[ Laughter ]

00:09:20.133 --> 00:09:22.434
And then you donate
the sweater to Goodwill,

00:09:22.434 --> 00:09:25.033
because she obviously
doesn't have any.

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:26.701
Now, you might

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:31.234
recognize the lawyer
in question.

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:32.701
His name is Eric Herschmann,

00:09:32.701 --> 00:09:34.400
and he's most famous
for testifying

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.100
before the January 6th committee
with a baseball bat on his wall

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:40.634
that says "justice", like
he's a middle school principal

00:09:40.634 --> 00:09:42.968
in a tough neighborhood
in a '90s movie.

00:09:42.968 --> 00:09:44.601
[ Deep voice ] You try
to sell crack in my school,

00:09:44.601 --> 00:09:48.133
and you'll live with a crack
in your skull, capisce?

00:09:48.133 --> 00:09:49.801
Now get out of my cafetorium.

00:09:49.801 --> 00:09:52.701
[ Normal voice ] He's either
a very intimidating lawyer

00:09:52.701 --> 00:09:54.267
or that's a piece of memorabilia

00:09:54.267 --> 00:09:55.767
he stole from
the Yankees clubhouse.

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:59.200
By the way, amazing week
for New York sports.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.934
Huge comeback win
for the Yankees last night.

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.934
The Mets clinched
the postseason.

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:04.801
The Jets pulled off
a miracle comeback.

00:10:04.801 --> 00:10:06.033
The Giants are 2-0.

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:08.334
It's a great time to be
a New York sports fan

00:10:08.334 --> 00:10:13.667
and a terrible time to host
a late night comedy show.

00:10:13.667 --> 00:10:15.100
And it's not just sports.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.067
I flew out of LaGuardia for
the first time in two years --

00:10:17.067 --> 00:10:21.100
and brace yourself, everybody --
it's super nice now.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:25.167
So I guess the monologue
is just, like, canceled forever.

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.434
LaGuardia is so nice now,

00:10:26.434 --> 00:10:28.400
even the New Yorkers
flying out of it are polite.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:29.567
I bumped into someone,

00:10:29.567 --> 00:10:31.000
because I was looking
at my phone and he said,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.133
"Excuse me, but could you please
pull your [Bleep] head

00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:35.934
out of your ass?"
I felt like I was in England.

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:37.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.200
Now, Trump's current
ridiculous argument

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.934
before he moves on
to what will certainly be

00:10:40.934 --> 00:10:42.868
an even more
ridiculous argument,

00:10:42.868 --> 00:10:45.601
is that he secretly
declassified the documents

00:10:45.601 --> 00:10:46.934
before leaving office.

00:10:46.934 --> 00:10:50.534
A Trump-picked right-wing
judge intervened

00:10:50.534 --> 00:10:52.334
to appoint what's called
a special master,

00:10:52.334 --> 00:10:53.868
basically a separate,
independent arbiter

00:10:53.868 --> 00:10:56.267
to go through and decide what
Trump should be allowed to keep.

00:10:56.267 --> 00:10:59.167
And that special master
held his first hearing

00:10:59.167 --> 00:11:00.801
with both sides yesterday,

00:11:00.801 --> 00:11:03.567
where he basically
slapped down the Trump team

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:05.701
for refusing to provide
any proof

00:11:05.701 --> 00:11:07.834
that Trump had actually
declassified the documents

00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:10.100
he said he had declassified.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.334
-Just a couple of hours ago,

00:11:11.334 --> 00:11:13.634
lawyers for the
Justice Department squared off

00:11:13.634 --> 00:11:16.400
with Donald Trump's legal team
for their first public

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.634
hearing before
Judge Raymond Dearie.

00:11:18.634 --> 00:11:21.534
He's the federal judge
who was appointed special master

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:23.834
to review the documents
seized in the search

00:11:23.834 --> 00:11:26.167
of Donald Trump's residence
last month.

00:11:26.167 --> 00:11:29.634
During this hearing, Dearie,
who was Donald Trump's pick --

00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:33.634
his hand-selected suggestion
to be the special master --

00:11:33.634 --> 00:11:36.734
told Donald Trump's lawyers
to put up or shut up on claims

00:11:36.734 --> 00:11:38.367
that Trump
declassified the records.

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:40.434
Here's how "Politico"
describes the hearing.

00:11:40.434 --> 00:11:41.434
Quote...

00:11:52.534 --> 00:11:53.534
Quote...

00:11:55.734 --> 00:11:58.667
-Well, I'm certain that metaphor
went right over Trump's head.

00:11:58.667 --> 00:11:59.667
[ Imitating Trump ]
If I have the cake,

00:11:59.667 --> 00:12:02.367
of course I'm gonna eat
the cake.

00:12:02.367 --> 00:12:04.267
Sleepy Joe, he want you
to order the cake

00:12:04.267 --> 00:12:05.534
and just look at the cake.

00:12:05.534 --> 00:12:08.100
But we're not gonna
let that happen, are we, people?

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:12.067
They want to take our guns,
our Twitter, and our cake?

00:12:12.067 --> 00:12:13.734
Both the dessert and the band.

00:12:13.734 --> 00:12:16.968
We love the band Cake,
don't we, folks?

00:12:16.968 --> 00:12:18.801
We love --
He's going the distance.

00:12:18.801 --> 00:12:20.067
He's going for speed.

00:12:20.067 --> 00:12:27.834
And she's all alone,
all alone in a time of need.

00:12:27.834 --> 00:12:29.367
Referencing Cake
and "The Honeymooners"

00:12:29.367 --> 00:12:32.834
in the same closer look,
it's risky.

00:12:32.834 --> 00:12:34.801
Neither is particularly fresh.
[ Laughs ]

00:12:34.801 --> 00:12:38.567
[ Laughter ]

00:12:38.567 --> 00:12:39.968
[ Normal voice ]
So the two leading contenders

00:12:39.968 --> 00:12:41.934
for the GOP nomination in 2024

00:12:41.934 --> 00:12:44.234
have sparked lawsuits
and criminal investigations

00:12:44.234 --> 00:12:46.234
and seem to be trying
to one-up each other

00:12:46.234 --> 00:12:47.400
in their corruption and cruelty.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.968
But so far,
Trump is way ahead of DeSantis

00:12:49.968 --> 00:12:51.133
when it comes to crimes.

00:12:51.133 --> 00:12:52.834
I don't know if Trump
is gonna end up in jail,

00:12:52.834 --> 00:12:55.300
but if he does, I bet they'll
try to break him out

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.067
by smuggling a nail file
inside a...

00:12:57.067 --> 00:12:59.033
-Cake.
-This has been...

00:12:59.033 --> 00:13:03.634
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.634 --> 00:13:05.234
...a closer look.

00:13:05.234 --> 00:13:08.267
♪♪

00:13:08.267 --> 00:13:10.000
The midterm elections
are coming up.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.934
So to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:13:12.934 --> 00:13:15.767
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:13:15.767 --> 00:13:19.801
to check your voter registration
status or to register to vote.

